diff --git a/public/ai/provider/gemini/UPGRADING.md b/public/ai/provider/gemini/UPGRADING.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..deeb8448de7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/public/ai/provider/gemini/UPGRADING.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# aiprovider_gemini Upgrade notes
+
+## 5.2.3
+
+### Added
+
+- A new `aiprovider_gemini\aimodel\gemini_image_base` interface has been added. Image generation model classes should implement this interface to declare which image generation protocol they speak (`PROTOCOL_IMAGEN` for the legacy Imagen `:predict` protocol, or `PROTOCOL_GENERATE_CONTENT` for the native Gemini `:generateContent` protocol) and the maximum number of images returned per request. For custom models without a model class, the protocol is inferred from the configured endpoint.
+
+  For more information see [MDL-89431](https://tracker.moodle.org/browse/MDL-89431)
+- New `gemini31flashimage` (gemini-3.1-flash-image), `gemini31flashliteimage` (gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image) and `gemini3proimage` (gemini-3-pro-image) model classes have been added for image generation using the native Gemini `generateContent` protocol. These replace the Imagen 4 models which Google is retiring on 17 August 2026.
+
+  For more information see [MDL-89431](https://tracker.moodle.org/browse/MDL-89431)
+
+### Changed
+
+- The default model for the "Generate image" action is now `gemini-3.1-flash-image`. Existing configurations using `imagen-4.0-generate-001` keep working until Google retires the endpoint, after which administrators should switch to one of the new Gemini image models.
+- `process_generate_image` now builds either an Imagen "predict" request body or a Gemini "generateContent" request body depending on the model's protocol, and parses the corresponding response schema. Gemini safety filtering (`promptFeedback.blockReason` and `candidates[0].finishReason`) is surfaced as an error response.
+
+  For more information see [MDL-89431](https://tracker.moodle.org/browse/MDL-89431)
